WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.850
I'm Kosta, and I run
Pinnacle Stone Restoration.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.090
We are specialized in
restoration of terrazzo

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.460
and natural-stone surfaces.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.860
I'm going to walk you
through how to restore

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.390
over-100-years-old terrazzo

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.269
that is covered in carpet.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.200
The most difficult part
of this restoration

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.930
is carpet and glue removal.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.405
We remove carpet with
electric scraping machines.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.590
It also can be done by hand,

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.176
but electric scraping machines

00:00:39.176 --> 00:00:42.002
do much faster and a better job.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.883
The project is taking place

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:47.370
in a historic university dormitory.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.890
The client decided to
restore existing terrazzo

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.810
rather than replacing carpet,

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.900
'cause carpet accumulates
a lot of dust and bacteria.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.960
Generally, terrazzo is
indestructible surface.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.393
Also, it's an easy maintenance.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.760
We are discovering multiple
issues with this terrazzo.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.520
Carpet glue, missing terrazzo,

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.310
surface cracks, and gouge nail holes.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.343
It's repairable but
requires a lot of work.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.900
The next step, we are
removing carpet glue.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.623
We are removing carpet glue
with handheld scrapers,

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.220
versus using grinding process.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.810
When we use a grinding process,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.450
we can activate the quality of the glue,

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.710
and it will become sticky.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.590
But by hand, we keep the temperature low,

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.973
and then glue, it just comes
out very easy from terrazzo.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.000
Then we grind terrazzo floors
with grinding machines.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.220
We use diamond disks.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:50.228
We use coarse, medium, and fine grits

00:01:50.228 --> 00:01:52.661
to flatten terrazzo.

00:01:52.661 --> 00:01:54.270
It's very important to level

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:57.060
and flatten terrazzo
floor for honing process

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.680
and before polishing process.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.390
In this particular project,

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.240
we are going to use a
dry-grinding process,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.180
just because we want to see the process.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.830
During the wet-grinding process,

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.320
the slurry that is produced
during the grinding

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.979
prevents us to see the
details of the terrazzo.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.480
After grinding process is completed,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.710
we're left with multiple
nail holes and cracks.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.660
To prepare them for patchwork,

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.850
we approach each like a dentist,

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.193
and we clean them out like a cavity.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.559
Then aggregates go into the holes.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.880
And when it cures, it will
be ready to be ground down,

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:46.055
to flatten, and to level it
to the existing terrazzo.

00:02:49.632 --> 00:02:52.260
The next step of restoration
process is honing,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.933
which is done with diamond pads.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:59.040
We use water, of course,
to lubricate the diamonds.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.260
So, lowest grit will be 50 grit,

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.778
followed by 120, 220,

00:03:03.778 --> 00:03:06.300
400, and 800 grit.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.010
What honing process does,

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.640
it ensures that no scratch is left behind

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.273
the grinding process.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.450
Since it's the wet process,

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.850
it will accumulate a lot of slurry

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:20.670
that has to be extracted by wet vacuums,

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.506
followed by edge work.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.498
So, edge work is the area that

00:03:26.498 --> 00:03:29.458
bigger machines don't
reach, those tight areas.

00:03:29.458 --> 00:03:32.250
So every step has to happen
with handheld machines

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.940
in a smaller scale, grinding
process to honing process,

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.470
to reach those tight areas

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.833
to develop the same sheen
as rest of the surface.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.160
The next step is a polishing.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.927
As 800 grit completes the honing process,

00:03:46.927 --> 00:03:49.680
1,500 grit starts polishing process.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.002
So, 1,500 grit followed by 3,000 grit.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.080
And after that, we use DIP systems.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.020
This is much finer diamond pads.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.850
When you polish terrazzo,

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.165
you're increasing the density of terrazzo,

00:04:05.165 --> 00:04:06.715
so it becomes more durable,

00:04:06.715 --> 00:04:09.039
because you're closing those pores.

00:04:09.039 --> 00:04:13.303
That automatically makes
terrazzo harder and more durable.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.620
And now it's time to seal.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.140
We're using microtopping sealer.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.873
It's more like impregnating sealer

00:04:20.873 --> 00:04:22.655
that goes into terrazzo,

00:04:22.655 --> 00:04:25.530
and it prevents terrazzo from staining,

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.450
and it protects it.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.460
The last step is burnishing.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.640
Burnishing helps sealer
to bring the terrazzo

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.669
to its highest sheen.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.410
If I had to compare this project

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.390
to other projects that we've done,

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.760
I would say this stands
for No. 10, for sure,

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.350
because there are a lot of obstacles

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:45.030
that we have to go through.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.610
And the terrazzo is original.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.252
And I have to mention that this is about

00:04:49.252 --> 00:04:51.060
5,000 square feet.

